# Append-only ledgers: let git union both sides instead of conflicting.
#
# sync-beta.yml merges main into beta on every main push, and both branches
# append to the bottom of these files — so every single sync collapsed into an
# append-append conflict. Measured 2026-08-12: EIGHT consecutive sync-beta
# failures in one evening, leaving beta 8 hours stale, which is exactly the rot
# that workflow exists to prevent.
#
# `union` keeps BOTH sides' lines rather than picking one, which is precisely
# right for a ledger nobody rewrites in place. It is deliberately NOT applied to
# code or to CLAUDE.md: there, a conflict is real information and silently
# unioning it would be how you lose work.
docs/DECISIONS-*.md merge=union
docs/STATUS.md      merge=union
